  "nonNavigableContext": "Water, wetlands, reed islands and far banks are scenic context. All connected cabin floor, both specimen pontoons, main deck and complete broad boardwalk are authored reachable surfaces; outer railings and specimen equipment have physical footprints.",
  "lessons": [
    "Open-air timber geometry distinguishes this wetland school from a conventional indoor laboratory.",
    "Whole connected pontoon widths are navigable rather than just narrow center routes.",
    "Only genuine chair-rail alpha belongs above native avatars; water, deck boards and reed shadows remain below.",
    "Original-art repair opened real full-width connections from the main deck to both side pontoons and removed the props at their approaches.",
